2026-09-28 — preserve include search classes in application command projection

Small source: include-projection/main.c plus two distinct selector.h files.
Original flags: -isystem system -Isystem -Iuser, also tested with joined
-isystemsystem. GCC14 documents that a directory occurring in both classes
keeps only its system position; user/selector.h must therefore win.
https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc-14.2.0/gcc/Directory-Options.html

RED against b34c17f application projectors:
  mixed, separated or joined: rewrites -isystem as -I; native exit 1.
  subject, joined: drops -isystemsystem; native exit 1.
  subject, separated: already retains the correct class; native exit 0.
  GCC14/Clang19 x O0/O2 x both spellings: all eight native controls exit 0.

GREEN: both adapters retain the search class and mapped operand. All four
projected native executions exit 0, and all eight reference controls remain
green. Joined -include/-isystem/-iquote/-imacros are split into their actual
option and single path operand, preserving spaces. Missing operands reach the
driver instead of being removed. Quote-only/macro-only options remain driver
refusals, not newly implemented features or ordinary include directories.
This is an adapter repair, not a new C preprocessing dialect.

All 314 ladder tests and targeted Ruff pass. The read-only original musl sweep
still parses all 1,339 sources with the current compiler; none of those original
records uses the changed include spellings, and no installed object changes.
It is not a new assembly, musl runtime, or full-benchmark receipt. Existing
diagnostic option omissions and other B08b boundaries remain open.

